@inject IStringLocalizer<SharedResource> Loc

@* Shown where a signed-in visitor has no Keyward profile yet, i.e. ICurrentUser.UserId is null.

   It exists because the alternative is worse than it looks: every feature page resolves the current user
   first and cannot do anything without it, so returning early leaves the page's LOADING placeholder standing
   for good. A permanent spinner reads as "slow", not as "misconfigured" — in a production incident that cost
   an hour of looking in the wrong place, while the actual cause (no tenant in the store this instance was
   pointed at, so the sign-in binding never created a profile) was one sentence away from being obvious.

   Deliberately no link to a status page: the route for that belongs to the host, not to this package. *@

<div class="card">
    <div class="empty-state">
        <KeywardIcon Name="alert" Size="28" />
        <p>@Loc["Common.NoKeywardAccount"]</p>
    </div>
</div>
